ace</span><span class="enc-snip">Hulbuk is the site of a medieval city in southern Tajikistan, at Kurbonshahid near Vose, identified as the capital of the principality of Khuttal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/huldrych-zwingli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Huldrych Zwingli</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Huldrych Zwingli was a Swiss priest and leader of the Reformation in Zürich.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/huliaipole"><span class="enc-name">Huliaipole</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Huliaipole is a town in Zaporizhzhia Oblast in south-eastern Ukraine.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hull-alfaro-treaty"><span class="enc-name">Hull–Alfaro Treaty</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1936</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hull–Alfaro Treaty was signed in 1936 by US Secretary of State Cordell Hull and the Panamanian envoy Ricardo J. Alfaro, and ratified by the United States in 1939.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hulu-guang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hulu-guang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hulü Guang</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hulü Guang was one of the leading generals of the Northern Qi dynasty in northern China, repeatedly defeating the rival Northern Zhou.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hulun-lake"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hulun-lake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hulun Lake</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hulun Lake is a large lake in Hulunbuir, in north-eastern Inner Mongolia, China, and one of the country's largest freshwater lakes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hulwan"><span class="enc-name">Hulwan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hulwan was an ancient and medieval town at the foot of the Zagros mountains, near modern Sarpol-e Zahab in western Iran, where the main road from Mesopotamia climbed…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/humaid-bin-abdullah-al-qasimi"><span class="enc-name">Humaid bin Abdullah Al Qasimi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Humaid bin Abdullah Al Qasimi was ruler of Ras al-Khaimah from 1869 to 1900.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/human-rights-act-1998"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/human-rights-act-1998.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Human Rights Act 1998</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Human Rights Act 1998 is a law of the United Kingdom that incorporated the rights of the European Convention on Human Rights into domestic law.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/human-sacrifice"><span class="enc-name">Human sacrifice</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Human sacrifice is the ritual killing of people as an offering to gods or spirits.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/humayun"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/humayun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Humayun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Humayun was the second Mughal emperor, son and successor of Babur, who ruled from 1530 to 1540 and again in 1555–1556.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/humayun-shah-bahmani"><span class="enc-name">Humayun Shah Bahmani</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Humayun Sh